// ROADMAP A16 prerequisite (2026-09-09), RELAYOUT: the fn cap is 768 and this
// construct sits just under it. c122_manyfns (521 fns) tests the OLD boundary --
// the b1_facts/b1_scratch aliasing that the 512 -> 560 raise exposed. This one
// tests the NEW one: after the relayout b1_facts is 2900..3667 (768 cells) and
// b1_scratch sits immediately above at 3668..3670, so an overrun at fn index 768
// lands on exactly the same two cells -- the B1 call-site counter and the
// skip-save flag -- and is exactly as silent. main() calls fns at indices 750 and
// 754, so the b1_facts entries nearest that edge are the ones under test.
// tools/check_abi.py's `perfn` gate is what makes the SIZE structural; this is
// what makes the BEHAVIOUR observable.
